Windrop is a Cygwin Windows port of Eggdrop IRC Bot

windrop-1.10.2.exe is a 7-Zip 26.03 self-extracting archive https://www.7-zip.org

$ sha256sum windrop-1.10.2.exe
4ac73d4ddb88bd6a649addc211890568e2030d54d66daaab4a1441f22e8b9418  windrop-1.10.2.exe

$ gpg --verify windrop-1.10.2.exe.sig windrop-1.10.2.exe
gpg: Signature made Mon 07 Sep 2026 04:06:52 AM CEST
gpg:                using RSA key 9117B74600C5801EE6616D86EEE2F7AD6B411573
gpg: Good signature from "Michael Ortmann (git sign) <ortmann@posteo.de>" [ultimate]

This Windrop includes:
- eggdrop 1.10.2 https://www.eggheads.org
- botnetop 1.5 module https://github.com/michaelortmann/botnetop.mod
- gseen 1.4.5 module https://github.com/michaelortmann/gseen.mod
- stats 1.15 module https://github.com/michaelortmann/stats.mod
- cygwin 3.6.10 https://cygwin.com
- openssl 4.0.2 https://openssl-library.org
- tcl 9.0.4 https://tcl.tk
- zlib 1.3.1 https://www.zlib.net
- 64 bit

Last official Windrop release was Windrop 1.8.3, so this alternative was
created until hopefully the official Windrop team resumes releasing new
versions.

Eggdrop: https://www.eggheads.org
Windrop: https://windrop.sourceforge.net

How to compile (steps to reproduce) Windrop 1.10.2:

Install Cygwin, select packages:
- autoconf2.7 2.73-1
- automake1.18 1.18.1-1
- binutils 2.47-1
- gcc-core 14.4.0-1
- git 2.51.0-1
- make 4.4.1-2
- mingw64-x86_64-gcc-core 14.4.0-1
- cygwins openssl can be used:
  libssl3 3.5.8-1 and openssl 3.5.8-1
  but i compiled openssl 4.0.2 instead
- cygwins tcl can be used:
  tcl 8.6.12-1 and tcl-devel 8.6.12-1
  but i compiled tcl 9.0.4 instead
- zlib-devel 1.3.2-1

Compile OpenSSL 4.0.2:
$ curl -LO https://github.com/openssl/openssl/releases/download/openssl-4.0.2/openssl-4.0.2.tar.gz
$ tar -zxf openssl-4.0.2.tar.gz
$ cd openssl-4.0.2
$ ./config no-docs no-apps --prefix=/opt/openssl-4.0.2
$ make
$ make install

Compile Tcl 9.0.4:
$ curl -LO http://prdownloads.sourceforge.net/tcl/tcl9.0.4-src.tar.gz
$ tar -zxf tcl9.0.4-src.tar.gz
$ cd tcl9.0.4/unix
$ ./configure --prefix=/opt/tcl-9.0.4
$ make
$ make install

Compile Eggdrop 1.10.2:
$ curl -LO https://github.com/eggheads/eggdrop/releases/download/v1.10.2/eggdrop-1.10.2.tar.gz
$ tar -zxf eggdrop-1.10.2.tar.gz
$ cd eggdrop
$ vi src/version.h
#   define EGG_PATCH "windrop"
$ cd src/mod
$ git clone --depth=1 https://github.com/michaelortmann/botnetop.mod.git
$ git clone --depth=1 https://github.com/michaelortmann/gseen.mod.git 
$ git clone --depth=1 https://github.com/michaelortmann/stats.mod.git
$ cd ../..

$ EGG=/opt/windrop-1.10.2
$ ./configure --prefix=$EGG --enable-strip --with-ssllib=/opt/openssl-4.0.2/lib --with-sslinc=/opt/openssl-4.0.2/include --with-tcllib=/opt/tcl-9.0.4/lib/libtcl9.0.dll.a --with-tclinc=/opt/tcl-9.0.4/include/tcl.h
$ make iconfig
#   enable webui
$ LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/openssl-4.0.2/lib:/opt/tcl-9.0.4/lib PATH=$PATH:/opt/openssl-4.0.2/bin:/opt/tcl-9.0.4/bin make eggd
rop
$ LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/openssl-4.0.2/lib:/opt/tcl-9.0.4/lib PATH=$PATH:/opt/openssl-4.0.2/bin:/opt/tcl-9.0.4/bin make inst
all
$ cp src/mod/botnetop.mod/botnetop.conf $EGG
$ cp src/mod/gseen.mod/gseen.conf $EGG
$ cp src/mod/stats.mod/stats.conf $EGG
$ cp -r src/mod/stats.mod/templates $EGG
$ cd $EGG
$ rm eggdrop.exe
$ mv eggdrop.exe-1.10.2 eggdrop.exe
$ rm -rf modules
$ mv modules-1.10.2 modules
$ cp /opt/openssl-4.0.2/bin/cygcrypto-4.dll .
$ cp /opt/openssl-4.0.2/bin/cygssl-4.dll .
$ cp /bin/cygwin1.dll .
$ cp /bin/cygz.dll .
$ cp /bin/cyggcc_s-seh-1.dll .
$ cp /opt/tcl-9.0.4/bin/cygtcl9.0.dll .
$ mkdir lib
$ cp -r /opt/tcl-9.0.4/lib/tcl9 lib
# BUG: cygwin 3.6.10 has got a bug, read(STDIN) results in 0 (eof), so
#   cygwin1.dll has been replaced with version 3.6.4

